  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: <img src=\"assets\\st0058_47979b32fb04.png\"><br>\nDue to \\(-\\mathrm{I}\\) and \\(-\\mathrm{R}\\) influence, \\(\\mathrm{NO}_2\\) in ortho-postion should have raised the acidity to the maximum extent. But it is due to intramolecular \\(\\mathrm{H}\\) - bonding, ortho-nitrophenol is less acidic than para - nitrophenol.<img src=\"assets\\st0058_b33114cf790a.png\"><br>"
